GTKGLTest @VERSION@ - riscos-gtk OpenGL test

A GtkGLArea drawing with OpenGL through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend and
riscos-mesa (EGL and OSMesa, rendering on the processor: OpenGL 2.1).

The window shows a spinning triangle on a blue background, and a white
square in its top left corner. The line underneath gives the renderer
and, once a second, the frame rate. Untick Spin to stop it.

Please check:
  - the triangle spins smoothly, and the white square is at the top
    left, not the bottom left;
  - resizing the window (toggle size, the size icon) keeps the picture
    filling the area;
  - another window dragged over it, or a menu opened over it, leaves no
    marks;
  - the frame rate at the window's starting size and when bigger;
  - in an EX0 EY0 (180 dpi) mode it is the same size and sharp.
Then send back the Log, <Wimp$ScrapDir>.GTKGLTest.Log, and a photo.

It needs RISC OS 5 in a 16 or 32 bpp mode, SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or
later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan).

